fucking files.
to declare a file: FILE *filename;
to OPEN a file: FILE *fopen(char*filename, char *opening_mode);
to CLOSE a file: int fclose(FILE*filename);

MODES of file opening
r -- opens a file-text for reading
w -- creates a file-text for writing
a -- annexes to a file-text
rb -- opens a binary file to read
wb -- creates a binary file to write
ab -- annexes to a binary file
r+ -- opens a file-text for reading/writing
w+ -- creates a file-text for reading/writing
a+ annexes or creates a file-text for reading/writing
r+b -- opens a binary file for reading/writing
w+b -- creates a binary file for reading/writing
a+b annexes to a binary file for reading/writing

the fopen() function
opens a file, remember to add an if incase the return of the function is NULL 
since that means that there was an error opening it.

the fclose() function
closes a file, returns 0 if no errors
if theres an error, it returns a value different than 0
receives as parameter a pointer to FILE
when fclose() is used, two pending datas on the buffer of the file are written
and the physical file is dissociated from FILE*
